ut " [:a {:href "/athletes/78811"} "Glenn Morris"] ", a former intermediate hurdler, contested his first decathlon in April at the Kansas Relays and broke the American record. At the combined AAU/Olympic Trials in 1936, he won with a world record of 7,880 on the new tables, with Clark second."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Clark led after the first day in Berlin, but Morris took the lead the next morning with the best time in the high hurdles, and he defeated Clark by almost 300 points with another world record of 7,900. " [:a {:href "/athletes/78876"} "Jack Parker"] " completed an American medal sweep. Morris never competed in another decathlon, leaving the event after three competitions, with three American records, two world records, and the Olympic gold medal. He later had a brief stint in the NFL and played “Tarzan” in one movie. " [:a {:href "/athletes/1200012"} "Leni Riefenstahl"] ", the controversial German film maker, also revealed that she and Morris had an affair during the 1936 Olympics."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Points (1952 Tables)"] [:th {} "Points (1962 Tables)"] [:th {} "Points (1985 Hand Tables)"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "801"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78811"} "Glenn Morris"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "7900"] [:td {} "7310"] [:td {} "7421"] [:td {} "7254"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "778"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78230"} "Bob Clark"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-ali